# udev rules for DataCore SANsymphony virtual disks served via iSCSI.
#
# Pins the block-layer I/O scheduler to `noop` on:
#   1. SCSI sd paths whose vendor is "DataCore" (the underlying iSCSI LUNs)
#   2. dm-multipath devices wrapping DataCore LUNs (WWID prefix 360030d90,
#      NAA type 6 + DataCore IEEE OUI)
#
# Why noop: XCP-ng 8.3 (kernel 4.19) defaults rotational SCSI devices to cfq,
# whose per-process queueing adds latency that's actively harmful on a
# low-latency iSCSI LUN served by DataCore's mirrored array. XAPI's own
# lvmoiscsi backend tunes the same way; this rule covers the SMAPIv3 path.
#
# Naming 99-* ensures we run after the distro/XCP-ng default rules so our
# setting wins. ACTION matches "add" (initial discovery) and "change"
# (re-detect after Serve/Unserve cycles, multipath reconfigure events).

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="sd*", \
  ATTRS{vendor}=="DataCore", \
  ATTR{queue/scheduler}="noop"

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="dm-*", \
  ENV{DM_NAME}=="?60030d90*", \
  ATTR{queue/scheduler}="noop"
